r nobody on file has, type the name if you know it and press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b>, or find the renter and press <b class="gd-ui">Link to</b> the name. The calls and texts so far follow the link. <b class="gd-ui">Match automatically again</b> undoes a link made by hand.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-missed-calls" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Missed calls</h2><p class="gd-p">A missed call raises the task &quot;Missed call from ...&quot; for the person on duty in customer service (whoever has Live chat or Texts and calls open), otherwise the customer service queue, and the Admins when nobody holds that function. In the quiet hours (11 pm to 7 am) the task is due at 7 am. One open task per number.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Quo itself texts back missed callers (its own auto-reply). The platform can do it instead (Program settings, &quot;Missed call: text the caller back&quot;), once per number in 12 hours: turn off Quo&#39;s own auto-reply first, or callers get two texts.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-and-texts-on-records" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls and texts on records</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s page and a booking&#39;s Messages &amp; history section show the texts, calls, missed calls, voicemails and summaries in the Activity log (chips <b class="gd-ui">Texts</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b>); an owner&#39;s page has &quot;Calls and texts&quot;. Calls are recorded: each call has its transcript and a one-line summary in the Activity log, and calls placed from the site&#39;s Call button are recorded too (below).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-activity-log-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Activity log (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s page and a booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Messages &amp; history</b> section have one <b class="gd-ui">Activity</b> log: everything about the renter, newest first, grouped by day. It holds the emails and account messages both ways and the emails the platform sent, the texts, the live chat, the calls with their summaries and next steps, the notes, the booking&#39;s events, the payments and refunds, the documents, identity checks and signatures, and the visits to the site with what they did there and the signals.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">All</b> shows everything. Press a chip (Emails, Texts, Live chat, Calls, Notes, Booking, Payments, Documents and ID, Website) to see one type; press <b class="gd-ui">All</b> to go back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type in <b class="gd-ui">Search the activity</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Search</b> to find a word in the log; <b class="gd-ui">Clear</b> takes it away.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">50 lines show at a time: <b class="gd-ui">Older</b> shows the next 50, <b class="gd-ui">Newest</b> goes back to the top.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Email</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> are at the top of the log. An email from the renter has <b class="gd-ui">Reply</b>, a text or call from them <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>, a chat line <b class="gd-ui">Open the chat</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b> is above the log; the note shows in it at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Payments show to Admins, customer service, Sales and Finance, as the booking&#39;s Money section. The log never shows an email address or a phone number.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-quo-contacts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Quo contacts</h2><p class="gd-p">Everyone on the site with a phone number is a contact in Quo under the same name, with their email and company: staff, renters and their drivers, owners, partners, investors, referral partners, job applicants, named visitors, leads, chauffeur clients, live chats, game players and forms left unfinished.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A new person is added within about five minutes; a changed name, phone or email is updated the same way. Change people on the site, not in Quo: the site&#39;s version is sent again.</li><li>One contact per number. When two records share a number, the strongest names the contact: staff, then a renter, a driver, an owner, a partner. A number without any name is not sent.</li><li>A contact someone already made in Quo for the number is updated rather than made twice, and its other numbers and emails are kept.</li><li>If Quo is down or slow, bookings and everything else go on; the contacts follow when it answers again.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Quo contacts</b>: how many are in Quo, waiting and in error, the last run and the last error, and <b class="gd-ui">Sync everyone again</b>. Program settings, &quot;Phone and texts (Quo)&quot;, turn it off.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-booking-texts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booking texts</h2><p class="gd-p">Since October 22, 2026 these are text alerts: each person chooses Email, Text or Both (the chapter Text alerts, below, and <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Text alerts</b>).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The settings</h2><p class="gd-p">Program settings, &quot;Phone and texts (Quo)&quot;: the line on or off, calls and texts kept, the missed-call text and its task, who calls back, AI suggestions and summaries with their daily neurons, the visit of a caller, and how long calls and texts of people who are not customers are kept (12 months).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-call-and-text-buttons" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call and Text buttons</h2><p class="gd-p">Every Call and Text button in Admin and the staff portal (a booking, a renter, the Now view, the map&#39;s cards, Visitors, the field jobs) goes through Quo, from the CarmaCars number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>: a small window opens with the person and the number. Write the text (sign it CarmaCars) and press <b class="gd-ui">Send</b>. It goes out from the CarmaCars number at once and is kept in the person&#39;s conversation under <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Visitors</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Chat</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Texts and calls</b>; press <b class="gd-ui">Open the conversation</b> to see it there. A number that asked for no texts is refused with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b>: on a phone the Quo app opens with the number in its dialer; press call there. On a computer the Quo web app opens in a new tab and the number is copied: open the dialer (Alt+C, or Ctrl+C on a Mac) and paste it. If Quo&#39;s desktop app is your computer&#39;s calling app, tick <b class="gd-ui">On this computer, call with the Quo desktop app</b> once: Call then opens it straight away. Every call is noted on the conversation as Call started from the site, and Quo adds the call itself when it ends.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Fleet, finance and field staff can call and text the people of their work (renters, owners, leads and staff); customer service and Sales any number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">To use the phone&#39;s own phone and messages apps instead, turn off <b class="gd-ui">Call and Text buttons go through Quo</b> in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>. With Phone and texts off, the buttons use the phone&#39;s own apps too.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-carmacars-app-links" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The CarmaCars app links</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, card The CarmaCars app (App Store and Google Play). Paste the App Store link (https://apps.apple.com/...) and the Google Play link (https://play.google.com/...) once the apps are live and press Save. From then on, iPhones and Android phones browsing the site see <b class="gd-ui">Download the CarmaCars app</b> in the footer and in the alerts invitation, with the link of their own store. Empty, nothing shows.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-who-is-calling-the-caller-pop-up-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who is calling: the caller pop-up (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">When someone calls the CarmaCars number, a panel opens at the bottom right of every Admin page (across the bottom on a phone) while the phone rings, and stays while the call goes on and for 3 minutes after it ends. Customer service get the same panel in their portal. The number is matched to the renter on file (their mobile or their account holder&#39;s), the same way Texts and calls matches it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A renter: their name, the booking on rent (or the next one coming) with the car, the balance they owe now (rental payments due and unpaid charges after a rental, <b class="gd-ui">overdue</b> when a payment is late), the deposit (held, waived, released, or not taken yet), what they are waiting on (a booking request or offer, a change, a question to them, an open To do) and the last three notes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write what the call was about in <b class="gd-ui">Note about this call</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add note</b>: it is kept on the renter with the time, your name and the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Open the renter&#39;s page</b> opens the full record. The booking opens from its line.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An unknown number shows <b class="gd-ui">Unknown caller</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Create lead</b> to keep it as a phone lead, then open the conversation in Texts and calls to name it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press the cross to close a call; it stays closed in this browser. The panel checks for calls every 10 seconds while you use the portal (once a minute when the page is left alone).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-through-the-site-open-the-pop-up-too-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls through the site open the pop-up too (release 48)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A call you place from the site (the Call button, the phone in your browser) opens the pop-up at once with the Call helper, for you only. It says <b class="gd-ui">Your call: on now</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Call ended</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A call to the CarmaCars number that rings the browsers opens the pop-up for everyone it rings (customer service and Sales, as set in Program settings), and for every Admin. When someone answers, it says <b class="gd-ui">On the phone now</b> and the history names who took it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The pop-up opens within about a second of the ring: it no longer waits for the 10 second check. Every office role gets it: customer service, Fleet, Sales and Finance.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Every call through the site is recorded (both sides), turned into text and summarised. On the renter&#39;s page, choose <b class="gd-ui">Calls</b> in the Activity log: each call shows the date, in or out, who took it, how long, <b class="gd-ui">Play</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Show the transcript</b> and the summary. The booking&#39;s history shows the same.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Quo calls show Quo&#39;s recording, transcript and summary there too. When Quo sends no summary, the site writes a one line summary from the transcript.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Calls of the last 60 days that were missing a recording, transcript or summary are looked up once at Twilio and at Quo, a few every five minutes.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-minimize-the-pop-up-and-the-call-helper-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Minimize the pop-up, and the Call helper (release 43)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The line at the top right of a call minimizes it to a small chip at the bottom of the page: the caller&#39;s name and the call&#39;s timer. A click anywhere outside the panel, or Esc, minimizes it too; nothing is closed by accident. Press the chip to open the call again. The cross still closes a call in this browser, and a new call always opens by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Inside each call, the <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b> is for new hires: <b class="gd-ui">Say</b> (the greeting, with the staff member&#39;s first name and the caller&#39;s name and booking when known), a button for each situation with 3 to 6 short steps and links to the right page of their portal, and <b class="gd-ui">Search the quick answers</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Hide</b> puts it away in that browser.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">You write all of it in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Call helper</b> (see Settings). <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on the helper takes you there.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-renter-notes-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter notes (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter page has <b class="gd-ui">Add a note</b>, and its Activity log lists the notes (chip <b class="gd-ui">Notes</b>): what staff noted about the renter, newest first, with the date and time, who wrote it and their role, the booking and the words during a call when it was written from the pop-up. Admins and office staff add notes; nobody can change one. To take one away, press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> and give the reason: it is no longer shown, and the note, the removal and the reason stay in the audit log. The same notes show on the caller pop-up, on a renter&#39;s conversation in Texts and calls, and on the staff portal&#39;s renter.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-the-call-button-through-twilio-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Call button through Twilio (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Since release 44 calls are made and taken in the browser (below); ringing the staff member&#39;s own cell first is a Program setting, off by default. The release 35 way: <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a staff page rings the staff member&#39;s own cell, then connects the customer with the CarmaCars number as caller ID, and logs the call with its length and outcome on the renter, lead or booking. It needs the GitHub secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_API_KEY and TWILIO_API_SECRET (and the CarmaCars number as a verified caller ID in Twilio); until then <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> opens Quo and says why. A staff member with no mobile on their profile is asked for it the first time they press <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> (a Canadian or US mobile, saved without a texted code), then the call starts (release 40).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-in-the-browser-release-44" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls in the browser (release 44)</h2><p class="gd-p">Staff, Admins included, make and take calls in the browser of the staff and Admin portals, with the CarmaCars number as caller ID. Staff abroad never use their own international number.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> anywhere opens a bar at the bottom left of the page: <b class="gd-ui">Calling ...</b>, then the timer, <b class="gd-ui">Mute</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Keypad</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Hang up</b>. The browser asks once for the microphone. The call is kept on the person&#39;s history with its length and its recording, as before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A call to the business number rings the browsers of the staff who have a staff page open, by role (customer service and Sales by default), each with <b class="gd-ui">Answer</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. Sales sees the caller&#39;s name or the number hidden.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Nobody online or nobody answered: the caller hears the message of Program settings and it is a missed call with its task and its text back, like every missed call. With a forward number set, the call goes there instead. Never to a staff member&#39;s own number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, the phone settings: <b class="gd-ui">Calls in the browser</b> (on), Whose browser rings (cs, sales; add admin, fleet or finance), <b class="gd-ui">Ring for (seconds)</b> (25), <b class="gd-ui">Calls in the browser: nobody answered, forward to</b> (empty), <b class="gd-ui">Calls in the browser: nobody answered, the message</b>, and Ring my own mobile first (the release 35 way, off).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Setting up Twilio once: save the GitHub repository secrets TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID (AC...), TWILIO_API_KEY (an API key SID, SK...), TWILIO_API_SECRET (that key&#39;s secret) and TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN (the account&#39;s Auth Token, which checks every request from Twilio), and TWILIO_CALLER_ID (the business number, for example +12895550123) when it differs from the CarmaCars number of Site settings. The business number must be a Twilio number or a verified caller ID in Twilio. The site makes the TwiML App &quot;CarmaCars browser calls&quot; itself, and points a Twilio business number with no Voice URL at the site. For incoming calls to ring browsers, calls to the business number must reach that Twilio number (buy it in Twilio, or forward to it). Until all is set, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> says what is missing.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Sales sees customer numbers hidden. Viewing as a Sales rep, <b class="gd-ui">Reveal</b> shows a number; every reveal is in the audit log.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-unanswered" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Unanswered</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Leads</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b> (customer service has it too): every customer text with no reply and every missed call not called back, oldest first. <b class="gd-ui">Reply</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Call back</b> opens the conversation; <b class="gd-ui">Mark answered</b> when it was answered another way. A customer waiting more than 15 minutes (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered SLA minutes</b>) alerts customer service and the Admins once. WhatsApp is not in the list: the morning digest reminds you to check it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-call-recording-and-transcripts-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call recording and transcripts (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Calls placed from the site&#39;s Call button are recorded from the moment the customer answers. No caller notice plays.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The recording is copied to CarmaCars&#39; private storage and deleted at Twilio once our copy is safe (Program settings, on by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">It is turned into text with the free daily AI allowance; when the allowance is used, the call waits for the next day.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The transcript, its summary and Play recording show on the renter&#39;s, the lead&#39;s, the booking&#39;s and the conversation&#39;s history, for Admins, customer service and Sales.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The transcript feeds the renter&#39;s and the lead&#39;s intent at once (hot, warm or cold, with what they said they want).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Recording and deleting at Twilio are two switches in Program settings, under the phone settings.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="texts-and-calls-the-quo-phone-line-calls-first-texts-after-release-37" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Calls first, texts after (release 37)</h2><p class="gd-p">Your main priority is always to be on the phone with people.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Answer a ringing call before anything else, and return a missed call at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Call before you text.</b> On a lead, a renter or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> is the first button and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> the second.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A text is a follow-up: after a call attempt (no answer, a voicemail left), or when the person asked for a text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On your To do and on <b class="gd-ui">Unanswered</b>, missed calls and call-backs are listed above unanswered texts.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
-- GUIDES 3451 END
